h Homebrew and quick install methods\n- Update project structure documentation\n\n* feat: add flexible configuration system for package users\n\n- Add priority-based config resolution:\n  1. --config flag (custom path)\n  2. ./deploy.env (per-project)\n  3. ~/.config/deploy-cli/ (global user)\n  4. DEPLOY_ROOT/config/ (installation default)\n- Add ''deploy init'' command to create config template\n- Add -c/--config flag for custom config path\n- Update help text with config locations\n- Update completions with new options\n\n* refactor: rename project from deploy-cli to shipctl\n\n- Update ASCII banner to SHIPCTL\n- Rename config directory to ~/.config/shipctl\n- Update all references in deploy.sh, README, CHANGELOG\n- Rename completions/deploy.bash to completions/shipctl.bash\n- Rename Formula/deploy-cli.rb to Formula/shipctl.rb\n- Update install.sh with shipctl branding\n- Update release workflow archive names\n- Update version output to ''shipctl version X.X.X''\n\n* chore: update CI pipelines with shipctl branding\n\n- Update GitHub Actions workflow header and name\n- Update GitLab CI pipeline comments and messages\n- Update Bitbucket Pipelines comments and messages\n- Reference shipctl init command in error messages\n\n* refactor: rename deploy.sh to shipctl\n\n- Rename main script from deploy.sh to shipctl\n- Update all CI pipelines (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket)\n- Update README, install.sh, Formula references\n- Update release workflow\n\n* docs: update CONTRIBUTING.md with shipctl branding\n\n- Replace deploy-cli references with shipctl\n- Update example commands to use shipctl","tree":{"sha":"b144c9e9881cf29bd39fea092e4f0847157b84c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/arramandhanu/shipctl/git/trees/b144c9e9881cf29bd39fea092e4f0847157b84c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/arramandhanu/shipctl/git/commits/cb6a46cb98f069f242db3b04d3b08b67190c5c33","verification":{"payload":"tree b144c9e9881cf29bd39fea092e4f0847157b84c9\nparent a59bdbfd7f2d4f4592d0b93bf4062